id: pm-vcs-ehvf
title: "Make the release gate deterministic: a clock-dependent changelog date and a branch V8 reported inconsistently"
description: "Two gates in this package passed or failed on something other than the code under test. The changelog heading for an unreleased version was stamped from the local calendar date, so a host at UTC+2 generating after 22:00 UTC produced tomorrow's date and CI regenerated today's, failing check on an otherwise identical commit. That defect was fixed upstream in pm-changelog 2026.8.2, but this package still pinned 2026.7.29-1 in its lockfile, so the fix had never actually arrived and the workaround of regenerating under TZ=UTC was being reapplied by hand. Separately the coverage gate failed at 99.49 percent branches on model.ts in one CI job while the other job on the same commit reported 100, and the same split appeared locally across runs. The cause was not flakiness in the gate: decodeTree had a genuinely uncovered arm, the non-array case of an entry line that parses as JSON, and V8 attributed that block as covered in some runs and not others. The gate was reporting a real gap intermittently rather than inventing one."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: "area:ci",determinism,release
created_at: "2026-08-03T00:36:21.288Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-03T00:36:30.083Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-03T00:36:30.070Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-03T00:36:30.070Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: "pm-changelog is upgraded to a version that derives release dates in UTC, and generating under TZ=UTC and TZ=Europe/Vienna at the same instant produces byte-identical output; the changelog no longer needs a TZ override to pass check; decodeTree refuses a tree entry line that parses to a non-array, covered by an explicit test for both an object and a scalar; three consecutive coverage runs report 100 percent lines, branches and functions with no variation; release:check exits zero end to end"
close_reason: "pm-changelog upgraded to 2026.8.2 and byte-identical output verified across TZ=UTC and TZ=Europe/Vienna at one instant; decodeTree's non-array arm covered for both an object and a scalar entry; three consecutive coverage runs reported 100/100/100 with no variation; release:check exits zero."
body: ""
